  "worked_solution": "The first term of an arithmetic series is ${a}_{1}=1.5$, the common difference is $d=3$, and the sum of the series is ${S}_{N}=150.$ Find the number of terms $N$ in the series.\n\nTo find the number of terms, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d).\n$$\n\nWe substitute ${a}_{1}=1.5$, $d=3$ and ${S}_{N}=150$ into the above and solve for $N$, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 150 & =\\frac{N}{2}(2\\cdot (1.5)+(N-1)\\cdot 3) \\\\ 150 & =\\frac{N}{2}(3+3N-3) \\\\ 150 & =\\frac{N}{2}(3N) \\\\ 150 & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot {N}^{2} \\\\ 100 & ={N}^{2} \\\\ N & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we take the positive square root because $N$ can't be negative.",
